# ComposeIO Composer Module Contracts [SPEC:CXC-MODULES]

> Implementation contracts for every Composer module. Each module is a `CTkFrame` subclass communicating via the internal ComposeIO bus. This document defines what each module does, what it subscribes to, what it publishes, and its behavioral contract.

---

## 1. Module Base Contract [CXC-MOD-BASE]

Every Composer module inherits from a common base:

```python
class ComposerModule(ctk.CTkFrame):
    MODULE_NAME: str                    # Human-readable name
    MODULE_MANIFEST: dict               # Declared subscriptions and publications

    def __init__(self, master, internal_bus, design_bus, design_state, **kwargs):
        ...

    def on_bus_ready(self):             # Called after all modules instantiated
        ...

    def on_design_loaded(self, design): # Called when a design file is loaded
        ...

    def destroy(self):                  # Unsubscribes from bus, cleans up
        ...
```

- `internal_bus`: The `composer-internal` bus for tool communication.
- `design_bus`: The live design bus for widget testing. May be None if module declares `design_bus: False` in manifest.
- `design_state`: Read-only reference to the `DesignDocument` data model. Modules read from it; mutations flow through bus commands only.

---

## 2. Palette Module [CXC-MOD-PALETTE]

### Contract

- role: Display the widget type catalog. Let the builder select a widget type for placement.
- class: `PaletteModule`
- position: Left sidebar (configurable).

### Manifest

```python
MODULE_MANIFEST = {
    "subscribes": ["composer/tool/mode", "composer/palette/catalog_changed"],
    "publishes": ["composer/palette/selected", "composer/palette/drag_start", "composer/palette/drag_end"],
    "design_bus": False,
}
```

### Behavior

| Trigger | Action |
|---|---|
| Startup | Query widget registry, populate catalog grouped by category |
| User clicks widget type | Publish `composer/palette/selected` with widget type name; switch tool mode to `place` |
| User drags widget type | Publish `composer/palette/drag_start`; on release, publish `composer/palette/drag_end` with drop coordinates |
| `composer/tool/mode` changes away from `place` | Deselect current palette selection |
| `composer/palette/catalog_changed` received | Refresh catalog from registry |

### Widget Registry Integration

The palette reads from the widget registry (`composer.widgets.registry`), which provides:

```python
@dataclass
class WidgetTypeInfo:
    type_name: str                      # "ButtonWidget", "GaugeWidget", etc.
    display_name: str                   # "Button", "Gauge"
    category: str                       # "input", "display", "container", "monitor"
    icon: str                           # Icon path or identifier
    default_properties: dict            # Default property values
    property_schema: dict               # Editable properties with types and constraints
    namespace_slots: list               # How many namespaces this widget consumes/produces
    preview_class: type                 # The actual CTkFrame class to instantiate in preview
    config_role: str                    # ComposeIO role this maps to (button-matrix, gauge-driver, etc.)
```

### Categories

| Category | Widgets | Description |
|---|---|---|
| Input | ButtonWidget, CoordinateEntryWidget | User interaction controls |
| Display | GaugeWidget, RelayWidget | State visualization |
| Monitor | BusMonitorWidget | Diagnostic / debugging |
| Container | Module Frame, ScrollableFrame | Layout grouping |
| ZB Widgets | SliderWithLabel, MetricsCardWidget, LogWidget, etc. | Plugin: zb_widgets library |

---

## 3. Canvas Module [CXC-MOD-CANVAS]

### Contract

- role: Visual layout surface. Display widget slots, module frames, binding connections. Handle drag, drop, resize, selection, and spatial arrangement.
- class: `CanvasModule`
- position: Center (main area).

### Manifest

```python
MODULE_MANIFEST = {
    "subscribes": [
        "composer/palette/selected", "composer/palette/drag_end",
        "composer/tool/mode", "composer/tool/snap_enabled", "composer/tool/grid_size",
        "composer/tool/show_bindings",
        "composer/config/widget_changed", "composer/config/module_changed",
        "composer/binding/created", "composer/binding/modified", "composer/binding/removed",
    ],
    "publishes": [
        "composer/selection/type", "composer/selection/widget_id",
        "composer/selection/module_id", "composer/selection/multi",
        "composer/selection/binding_id",
        "composer/canvas/widget_added", "composer/canvas/widget_removed",
        "composer/canvas/widget_moved", "composer/canvas/widget_resized",
        "composer/canvas/module_added", "composer/canvas/module_removed",
        "composer/canvas/layout_changed", "composer/canvas/viewport",
        "composer/command/execute",
    ],
    "design_bus": False,
}
```

### Visual Elements

| Element | Representation | Interaction |
|---|---|---|
| Widget slot | Rounded rectangle with icon, type name, namespace label, and LED indicator color | Click to select, drag to move, corner handles to resize |
| Module frame | Container rectangle with header bar (module name, role badge) | Click header to select module, drag header to move module, edge handles to resize |
| Binding arrow | Directed curve from source widget to target widget, labeled with transform type | Click to select binding, delete key to remove |
| Grid overlay | Dotted lines at `grid_size` intervals | Shown when `snap_enabled` is on |
| Alignment guide | Solid colored line appearing during drag | Snap feedback when widget edge aligns with another |

### Canvas Coordinate System

- origin: Top-left of the canvas content area.
- units: Logical pixels (1:1 with screen pixels at 100% zoom).
- zoom: Canvas supports zoom via scroll wheel. Viewport published to `composer/canvas/viewport`.
- pan: Pan via middle-mouse-drag or `pan` tool mode.
- infinite canvas: No fixed boundary. Scrollable in all directions.

### Grid Snap Behavior

When `composer/tool/snap_enabled` is on:
- Widget positions snap to nearest grid intersection on drop/move.
- Widget sizes snap to nearest grid multiple on resize.
- Module frame positions snap to grid.
- Grid size controlled by `composer/tool/grid_size` (default: 10px).

### Module Frame Rules

| Rule | Description |
|---|---|
| Widgets must be inside a module | Dropping a widget on bare canvas creates a default module frame first |
| Modules cannot overlap | Dragging a module into another's space is blocked or auto-adjusts |
| Widgets cannot span modules | A widget belongs to exactly one module |
| Module layout is grid-based | Widgets within a module use grid layout (row/col) |
| Design layout is grid-based | Modules within the design use grid layout with configurable weights |

---

## 4. Property Editor Module [CXC-MOD-PROPERTY]

### Contract

- role: Display and edit properties of the currently selected object (widget, module, binding, or namespace).
- class: `PropertyEditorModule`
- position: Right sidebar (configurable).

### Manifest

```python
MODULE_MANIFEST = {
    "subscribes": [
        "composer/selection/type", "composer/selection/widget_id",
        "composer/selection/module_id", "composer/selection/binding_id",
    ],
    "publishes": [
        "composer/config/widget_changed", "composer/config/module_changed",
        "composer/config/namespace_changed",
        "composer/command/execute",
    ],
    "design_bus": False,
}
```

### Property Editor Modes

The property editor's content changes based on `composer/selection/type`:

#### Mode: `none` (Design Properties)

| Property | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| Design name | text | Human-readable design name |
| Target platform | enum: [desktop, cyd_320x240, cyd_480x320, custom] | Target display resolution |
| Bus config | group | Default scope, authority settings |

#### Mode: `widget` (Widget Properties)

Dynamically populated from the selected widget's `property_schema`. Common properties across all widget types:

| Property | Type | Editor | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| widget_id | text (auto-generated, editable) | Text field | Unique identifier |
| namespace | namespace picker | Dropdown + create new | Primary namespace for this widget |
| label | text | Text field | Display label |
| state_engine | engine picker | Dropdown + custom enum editor | State engine for this widget's namespace |
| input_type | enum: [toggle, momentary, hold_and_ramp, rotary] | Dropdown | Input mechanic (input widgets only) |
| led_behavior | enum: [follow_state, blink_500ms, while_pressed, solid, off] | Dropdown | LED indicator behavior (input widgets only) |
| scope | enum: [local, global, remote, auto] | Dropdown | Namespace scope |

Widget-type-specific properties are appended below common properties, sourced from the widget's `property_schema`.

#### Mode: `module` (Module Properties)

| Property | Type | Editor | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| module_id | text | Text field | Module identifier |
| module_type | text (read-only) | Label | Module role type |
| role | enum per [SPEC:CIO-CONFIG-SCHEMA] | Dropdown | ComposeIO role (button-matrix, relay-controller, etc.) |
| scope | enum: [local, global, auto] | Dropdown | Default scope for all widgets in module |
| columns | integer | Spinner | Number of grid columns within the module |
| padding | dimension | Spinner | Internal padding |

#### Mode: `binding` (Binding Properties)

Varies by binding type (simple, compound, event_triggered). See [SPEC:CIO-CONFIG-SCHEMA] for full binding config.

| Property | Type | Editor | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| binding_id | text | Text field (read-only) | Auto-generated ID |
| type | enum: [simple, compound, event_triggered] | Dropdown | Binding type |
| input_namespace(s) | namespace picker | Dropdown(s) | Source namespace(s) |
| output_namespace | namespace picker | Dropdown | Target namespace |
| transform | transform editor | Visual chain builder | Transform pipeline |
| conditions | condition editor | Visual rule cards (compound only) | Conditional rules |

### Editor Types

| Editor Type | Widget | Used For |
|---|---|---|
| Text field | `CTkEntry` | Strings, identifiers |
| Dropdown | `CTkOptionMenu` | Enum values, fixed choices |
| Spinner | `CTkEntry` + increment/decrement buttons | Integers, dimensions |
| Color picker | Swatch button + color dialog | LED colors, theme colors |
| Namespace picker | Dropdown of registered namespaces + "create new" option | Namespace assignment |
| State engine picker | Dropdown (binary, tri_level, etc.) + custom enum editor | State engine selection |
| Transform chain builder | Vertical stack of transform cards with add/remove | Transform pipelines |
| Condition card editor | Vertical stack of when/value pairs | Compound binding conditions |

### Property Change Protocol

1. User modifies a value in the editor.
2. Editor validates the new value against the property's type constraints.
3. If valid: publish `composer/config/widget_changed` (or `module_changed`, `namespace_changed`) with old and new values.
4. Simultaneously publish `composer/command/execute` with undo data.
5. If invalid: show inline validation error; do not publish.

---

## 5. Binding Editor Module [CXC-MOD-BINDING]

### Contract

- role: Create, edit, and visualize namespace bindings (simple, compound, event-triggered).
- class: `BindingEditorModule`
- position: Bottom panel or tab alongside Property Editor.

### Manifest

```python
MODULE_MANIFEST = {
    "subscribes": [
        "composer/selection/type", "composer/selection/widget_id",
        "composer/selection/binding_id",
        "composer/canvas/widget_added", "composer/canvas/widget_removed",
        "composer/config/namespace_changed",
    ],
    "publishes": [
        "composer/binding/created", "composer/binding/modified",
        "composer/binding/removed",
        "composer/command/execute",
    ],
    "design_bus": False,
}
```

### Binding Creation Modes

#### Visual Drag-Connect (Canvas Integration)

1. User switches to `connect` tool mode.
2. User clicks source widget on canvas → source namespace highlighted.
3. User drags to target widget → binding arrow drawn.
4. On release: Binding Editor opens pre-populated with source and target namespaces.
5. User configures transform/conditions → publishes `composer/binding/created`.

#### Binding List Mode

1. Binding Editor shows all bindings in the design as a scrollable list.
2. Each binding is a card showing: source → transform → target.
3. Click card to select and edit.
4. "Add Binding" button opens blank binding form.

### Binding Types

#### Simple Binding Card

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  Simple Binding                    [Delete] │
│                                             │
│  Source: [sublight_engines    ▼]            │
│  Target: [gauge_power         ▼]            │
│                                             │
│  Transform:                                 │
│  ┌─────────────────────────────┐            │
│  │ map: off→0, half→50, full→100│  [Edit]  │
│  └─────────────────────────────┘            │
│  [+ Add Transform Step]                     │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

#### Compound Binding Card

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  Compound Binding                  [Delete] │
│                                             │
│  Output:   [ftl_jump_led      ▼]           │
│  Requires: [ftl_arm == "on"      ]          │
│  Default:  [off               ▼]           │
│                                             │
│  Conditions:                                │
│  ┌─────────────────────────────────────┐    │
│  │ WHEN ftl_cap_charge < 50            │    │
│  │ VALUE: blink_fast              [x]  │    │
│  ├─────────────────────────────────────┤    │
│  │ WHEN ftl_cap_charge >= 50           │    │
│  │  AND ftl_coord_status == committed  │    │
│  │ VALUE: solid                   [x]  │    │
│  └─────────────────────────────────────┘    │
│  [+ Add Condition]                          │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

#### Event-Triggered Binding Card

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  Event-Triggered Binding           [Delete] │
│                                             │
│  Trigger: [ftl_jump.event == "jump"  ]      │
│  Output:  [ftl_jump_led      ▼]            │
│  Set to:  [off               ▼]            │
│                                             │
│  Side Effects:                              │
│  ┌─────────────────────────────────────┐    │
│  │ SET ftl_arm = off              [x]  │    │
│  │ SET ftl_cap_charge = 0         [x]  │    │
│  │ SET ftl_coord_status = dark    [x]  │    │
│  └─────────────────────────────────────┘    │
│  [+ Add Side Effect]                        │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

### Transform Editor

Available transform types (from [SPEC:CIO-CONFIG-SCHEMA]):

| Transform | Editor | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `map` | Key-value table | Map discrete values: `{"off": 0, "on": 255}` |
| `scale` | Min/max fields | Linear scale: `{min: 0, max: 100, out_min: 0, out_max: 255}` |
| `threshold` | Value + above/below fields | Binary threshold |
| `deadzone` | Center + range fields | Ignore small changes around center |
| `debounce` | Duration field | Suppress rapid changes |
| `invert` | Toggle | Reverse value |

Transforms are chained vertically. Output of one feeds input of next.

