## 6. Namespace Inspector Module [CXC-MOD-NAMESPACE]

### Contract

- role: Display all namespaces in the design, their state engines, current values (from design bus), publishers, and subscribers.
- class: `NamespaceInspectorModule`
- position: Bottom panel or tab.

### Manifest

```python
MODULE_MANIFEST = {
    "subscribes": [
        "composer/canvas/widget_added", "composer/canvas/widget_removed",
        "composer/config/namespace_changed",
        "composer/binding/created", "composer/binding/modified", "composer/binding/removed",
        "composer/connection/discovery",
    ],
    "publishes": [
        "composer/selection/type", "composer/selection/binding_id",
        "composer/config/namespace_changed",
    ],
    "design_bus": True,  # Subscribes to all design bus namespaces for live values
}
```

### Display

```
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  Namespaces                                                  [+New] │
│                                                                     │
│  Name              Engine          Value     Publishers  Subscribers │
│  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│  ftl_arm           binary          off       btn_001     relay_001  │
│  ftl_cap_charge    continuous      0         (timer)     gauge_001  │
│  ftl_coord_status  enum(5)         dark      coord_001   bind_002   │
│  ftl_jump          (event)         —         btn_005     bind_003   │
│  ftl_jump_led      enum(4)         off       bind_002    relay_002  │
│  sublight_engines  tri_level       off       btn_002     bind_001   │
│  gauge_power       continuous      0         bind_001    gauge_002  │
│  ⚡ red_alert      binary          off       [hardware]  —          │
│                                                                     │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

- live-values: The "Value" column updates in real-time from the design bus. When hardware is connected, values reflect actual hardware state.
- hardware-namespaces: Namespaces discovered from hardware modules (via `discovery` messages) are marked with a lightning bolt icon. These are read-only in the inspector — they're defined by hardware config, not the Composer.
- click-to-select: Clicking a namespace row publishes `composer/selection/type = namespace` and populates the Property Editor with namespace config.

